items.Weapon_Crossbow_AS_SMG_Funeral_Procession.description = A Mournhollow reliquary key seats behind a violet chamber. Its inscriptions are names, each left unfinished until the living return. Short-range automatic pressure; steep travel falloff and frequent reloads.\n6/8.5 body/head before class, enchantments and armor. 0.24s cycle; 22 rounds; F reload 2.55s.\nHold primary for automatic fire; secondary aims. Uses only Gravelight Compact Rounds. Ammo transfers at reload completion.\nFull base damage through 10 blocks of actual projectile travel, falling to 25% at 72. Nominal travel limit 55 blocks.
items.Weapon_Crossbow_AS_SMG_Grindhymn.name = Grindhymn, the Gobliterator's Encore
items.Weapon_Crossbow_AS_SMG_Grindhymn.description = The Gobliterator's broken heart turns within an amber lattice. Deepworks smiths listened to the wreckage and forged its stubborn rhythm into a weapon. Cyan rails flare between battered iron ribs; every discharge is followed by the scrape and sigh of machinery forced to remember its purpose. Short-range automatic pressure; steep travel falloff and frequent reloads.\n8/10 body/head before class, enchantments and armor. 0.26s cycle; 24 rounds; F reload 2.9s.\nHold primary for automatic fire; secondary aims. Uses only Cindercoil SMG Cells. Ammo transfers at reload completion.\nFull base damage through 10 blocks of actual projectile travel, falling to 25% at 72. Nominal travel limit 50 blocks.\nQ — Grinding Halt: 18/23 body/head, costs 2 rounds; 12s shared special cooldown; 1.6s recovery. Hold Q for 0.8s to fire one focused shot; eligible NPCs stagger for 0.55s. Freeze immunity and enraged interrupt immunity prevent the stagger. The shot commits two loaded rounds and locks firing for 1.6s. Releasing before the charge completes cancels without spending rounds or starting the special cooldown.
items.Weapon_Crossbow_AS_SMG_Starling.name = Starling, Chorus of First Light
items.Weapon_Crossbow_AS_SMG_Starling.description = Three fragments of Luminia's fallen seals lie aligned within a pale prism. White-gold channels awake around a violet star, casting the small light once kept above the sanctum doors. Its bearer inherits an unfinished vigil: guide the faithful through the dark, and spend the dawn with care. Short-range automatic pressure; steep travel falloff and frequent reloads.\n5.5/13.5 body/head before class, enchantments and armor. 0.26s cycle; 24 rounds; F reload 2.9s.\nHold primary for automatic fire; secondary aims. Uses only Vesperglass SMG Cells. Ammo transfers at reload completion.\nFull base damage through 10 blocks of actual projectile travel, falling to 25% at 72. Nominal travel limit 72 blocks.\nQ — Firstlight Refrain: 6/10 body/head, costs 2 rounds; 12s shared special cooldown; 1.6s recovery. Press Q for a low-damage setup shot that visibly marks NPCs for 2s and slows eligible NPCs by 35% for 1s. Slow-immune NPCs retain only the visual mark. The shot commits two loaded rounds and locks firing for 1.6s.
